    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two premier assets: **Junior Caminero** (74.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.67). **Junior Caminero** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly, where his +19% SP skill bonus and advantageous #3 spot in the order make him the primary engine of our offense. Simultaneously, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite a neutral park factor; his elite .444 xwOBA against Jack Flaherty makes him an immovable force in the outfield. **Trea Turner** (70.97) also warrants high expectations, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Cionel P\u00e9rez and the #1 order slot provide a massive ceiling for stolen base potential, a critical metric for our roster construction.\n\nStrategic deployment today focuses on high-upside speed and situational efficiency. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.08) earns a standout grade largely due to Brandon Woodruff\u2019s slow delivery, which grants him a +4% boost to his SB probability\u2014a crucial edge in our scarcity-driven strategy. While **Lars Nootbaar** (58.33) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.05) sit in the middle of our scoring distribution, both are preferred over the bench options, including **Luke Raley** (47.07), who narrowly missed the cut. **Luke Raley** was the strongest candidate for promotion, but his diminished SP skill rating against Gavin Williams and a lower-order projection relegated him to the bench. We must remain vigilant regarding the pending lineups; should **Gary Sanchez** or **Christian Yelich** shift down in their respective orders, their efficiency scores will likely regress, necessitating a potential pivot to our deeper utility options.",
